  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-41302-IP24-SAU106</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41302" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Labour Organization (ILO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved skills governance for better employability and employment outcomes in Saudi Arabia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ILO will provide technical assistance to the Ministry of Human Resources and Social Development (MHRSD) to develop skills and a lifelong learning system responsive and inclusive. This will enable individuals to acquire competencies for a decent job, support sustainable enterprises and contribute to economic growth. This will skills system through; i) formulation of market responsive and inclusive; ii) future skills development policy with a focus on institutionalized private sector engagement, iii) institutional capacity for skills anticipation and skills match, and iv) development of occupational competency standards, career guidance and apprenticeship. 
The ILO will also work with the Agency for Skills and Training, to support its efforts concerning skills development and enhanced employability. This would be done through a combination of technical assistance and capacity-building activities to increase their knowledge of the policy development process, from preparation to monitoring and evaluation.  
The ILO will also support the delivery of training on employment impact assessment for relevant MHRSD staff which would help participants develop a theory of change and select indicators to measure job-related outcomes and impact; identify the most suitable method to assess a given type of employment promotion intervention; and design Employment Impact Assessments that consider both the quantity and quality dimensions of employment, as well as the needs of specific groups such as youth, women, rural populations and informal workers.</narrative>
  </description>
